    "manufacturer_status": "abandoned",
    "name": "Magic Display",
    "notes": "Bluetooth-controlled LED displays for shoes, bags, hats, crafts. Uses Quintic (NXP QN-series) BLE chipset with QPP (Quintic Private Profile) on service 0xFEE9. All BLE traffic is AES-128 encrypted via native libAES.so (key in .so binary, not in Java). Commands are fixed 16-byte ASCII-named packets: [length, ASCII_CMD..., params..., zero_pad]. Bulk data uses 3-way handshake: DATS -> DATSOK -> 16-byte frames -> DATCP -> DATCPOK. Supports multiple display sizes: 5x36, 12x48, 14x56, 16x64 (reported via STYPE response). Monochrome 1-bit-per-pixel bitmap encoding (threshold: any RGB channel >= 128 = ON). Device identification by manufacturer-specific adv data: {0x54, 0x52, 0x00, 0x27} (\"TR\" + 0x0027). No pairing required. Also has OTA service at 0xFEE8 (Quintic OTA protocol).\n",
    "protocol": "ble"
  },
